Gemma 4 26B-A4B NVFP4 with MTP assistant, 18 concurrent sessions, one DGX Spark (vLLM)

Vendored upstream files (byte-identical, provenance spelling upstream-<name>):
  upstream-README.md, upstream-start.sh, upstream-stop.sh, gemma4.py
from https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/Gemma-4-26B-A4B-DGX-Spark-18-concurrencies
at commit 39e94192bd6f114a222d434cf2bf4dcf173248a5.

The upstream repository carries no licence file (GitHub reports none); its
terms are unspecified. gemma4.py is a modified copy of vLLM's
vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4.py and keeps its Apache-2.0 header (vLLM
project, Google Inc., HuggingFace Inc.). Upstream bind-mounts it over the
image's copy; the build here copies the same file over the base image's copy.
Against vLLM v0.25.1 the difference is small: it replaces
lm_head.tie_weights(embed_tokens) with a direct weight share (ModelOpt does not
implement tie_weights) and predates the mm_prefix_clamp_sliding_window argument.

Our files: Dockerfile, vllm-wrapper.sh, verify-runtime.py and this notice.

The models, nvidia/Gemma-4-26B-A4B-NVFP4 and google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-assistant,
are published under Google's Gemma terms (the model cards point to
https://ai.google.dev/gemma/apache_2 and
https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/gemma_4_license). vLLM is Apache-2.0.
